#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""claude-agents-lane: keep agent work in agents.slice, behind your apps.

Agent work is the Claude Code daemons, their sessions and subagents, and everything they start: test runs, headless
browsers, MCP servers, a memory worker. It used to share app.slice with your own apps at the same CPU weight (100), so
under load the compositor's D-Bus thread waited behind it. agents.slice (CPUWeight=20, next to this file) ranks agent
work behind your apps.

A slice only ranks what is inside it, and nothing starts a Claude inside this one: a Claude is born in the cgroup of
whatever started it, usually a Konsole tab's scope, and everything it spawns later stays there with it. So this tool
moves what runs outside the lane into it. It is run when a Claude window opens (claude-window asks for a round and does
not wait for it) and every minute (claude-agents-lane.timer), because a daemon respawned by any other path lands in
that caller's group.

  adopt [--dry-run] [--json]   move every Claude Code tree that runs outside agents.slice into a scope of its own
                               inside it; one line per scope, nothing when there is none (--dry-run also says which
                               trees it would leave where they are)
  status [--json]              the lane's weight, how many agent processes are in it, how many a round would move,
                               which trees it leaves, and the lane's share of the CPU over a 2 s sample

What is a root:

  - A Claude: a process of your user manager (user@<uid>.service) whose EXECUTABLE is a file directly in your install
    folder, ~/.local/share/claude/versions/ (the home from the password database, never $HOME), and that runs under
    one of Claude's names. The executable says what a process is, the command line only which kind: `claude daemon`,
    `claude bg-<helper>`, or a session (no subcommand: `claude`, `claude --resume ...`,
    `claude -p ...`). Never comm, which is the version string for sessions. The bundled `ugrep` is Claude's
    executable under another name and is no Claude; an executable that cannot be read is nobody's.
  - A look-alike is no Claude either: a file named claude anywhere else, or in some other claude/versions folder. It
    is never moved, only counted ("lookalikes" in the JSON): if Claude's installer ever moves, the lane takes nothing,
    and that count is what shows it.
  - The claude-mem worker, in the one form that runs here: bun, bun.exe or node whose argv[1] itself is a
    worker-service.cjs in your home, below a `plugins` folder and then a `claude-mem` one. Anything else is no worker.
  - Never a client: a Claude with the argument `attach` (it draws a window you type into) or `agents` (the hub's short
    polls) anywhere before a bare `--`. A client is not a root, and below a root it is not taken along either.
  - Never any other subcommand (stop, logs, mcp, update, ...), a `claude ... --bg` client, `--version` or `--help`.
  - Nothing outside your user manager.

What moves, and what stays:

  - A tree is the top-most root and its descendants. Ancestors stay: a session under a shell moves, the shell and its
    Konsole do not. A window of yours below a root stays as well, with what runs below it.
  - Only out of scopes. A service is run by its unit: its stop, its restart and its KillMode rules are all about the
    processes in its cgroup, so a tree in a service is left there and counted.
  - Only from the units of your windows (your terminal window and a chat app, told by their executable): the unit a
    window runs in, when that unit is named after it, and the unit it was launched in (run-p<pid>-i<n>.scope, which
    `systemd-run --scope` makes). A root outside the lane is taken only from such a unit.
  - Strays, every round: a descendant of a root that already lives in the lane, found outside it in such a unit, goes
    into a new scope of its own.
  - Everything else was put where it is on purpose (`systemd-run --scope -p MemoryMax=...`, snapd). It stays and is
    counted ("placed", and "placed_trees" for whole agent trees: the number to watch), never named.
  - A scope in the lane is not part of the graphical session, on purpose: a Claude outlives a logout (lingering is on).

How a move is made, by your user manager, over the session bus:

  - A move never names a process by its number. Each process is first HELD (a pidfd) and then looked at again: only
    one that still has the start time it was scanned with, is not a zombie, and is still what the scan decided by (its
    cgroup, comm, executable and arguments) is handed over, as that pidfd (StartTransientUnit with PIDFDs). The tree's
    root is held first and looked at once more, last, after every member of the piece. A root that changed ends its
    tree for the round. Nothing is ever added to a scope that exists.
  - The manager itself checks each descriptor and then acts on the number, two system calls apart; that gap is the
    manager's, and a number comes round again only after pid_max others.
  - In pieces of 16: one message on the session bus carries 16 file descriptors (dbus-daemon's built-in limit). A
    bigger tree moves in several scopes in the same round, the root's last.
  - A process that ends under the call fails the call, which is then made again with the ones still there, a few
    times. What a round does not get, the next one finds.
  - A round has a deadline of its own, 25 s from its start: no piece and no retry starts after it, and what is left is
    the next round's (one line on stderr, the same in "errors", exit 1).
  - It never stops, restarts or changes a unit. A scope goes when its last process has gone.

The lane pass, in every round of adopt that is not a dry run (harden_lane):

  - Every process the scan found in the lane gets its oom_score_adj raised to 400 when it is a Claude Code process and
    to 600 when it is anything else, and its soft core-file limit and its soft realtime-priority limit set to 0 (the
    hard limits stay). KWin sits at 200, so the lane loses before the desktop does. A value is only ever raised, never
    lowered, and a process that has it all gets no call.
  - Once per round, in adopt only (never in a dry run, never in status), and it runs before the first move, so a tree is
    hardened in the round after the one that moves it. Its time is at most 5 s of the round's 25 s.
  - It prints nothing and has no part in the report or the exit status.
  - Left alone: a zombie, a process that is not yours, one whose executable or arguments cannot be read, your windows
    and the clients that draw in them, and what runs below them up to the first agent root on the way up.
  - prlimit is the one call in this tool that names a process by its number; each process is held by a descriptor on
    its /proc/<pid> directory and looked at through it before and after the call.
  - It is inherited: everything an agent starts later gets the same adj and limits wherever it runs. Launchers start
    their window with `systemd-run --user --scope`, which execs in place, so the window keeps the agent's values. A
    part of your desktop that an agent restarts has to be restarted with `systemctl --user restart`, so your own
    manager starts it with its own settings.
  - No core files from a nested session an agent runs, even with CLAUDE_HUB_NESTED_CORES=1: that switch only skips the
    script's own `ulimit -c 0`. A core file there needs a run outside the lane with `ulimit -c unlimited`.
  - Undo: revert the change. A raised oom_score_adj can be written back by the same user (typically to 200).

Never a command line in the output or in a scope's description: kinds, pids, counts and unit names only.

Test switches: CLAUDE_HUB_AGENTS_LANE_PROC (a fake /proc), CLAUDE_HUB_AGENTS_LANE_UID, CLAUDE_HUB_AGENTS_LANE_CGROUP (a
fake /sys/fs/cgroup, for status), CLAUDE_HUB_AGENTS_LANE_RECORD (a file: every call to the mover is appended to it as
a JSON line instead of reaching the bus, and the fake /proc's cgroup files are rewritten the way the manager would).
RECORD also feeds the lane pass's hardener. A fake /proc without a RECORD file never gets a mover or a hardener. The
hardener refuses the real /proc under any other name and writes a rehearsal folder only when it holds the marker file
claude-agents-lane-fake-proc, which no procfs can hold.

A round costs one scan of /proc and imports nothing heavy (no argparse, dataclasses, pathlib or D-Bus bindings until
there is something to move): it runs every minute.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import os
import pwd
import resource
import sys
import time

SLICE = "agents.slice"
WANTED_WEIGHT = 20
SYSTEMD = ("org.freedesktop.systemd1", "/org/freedesktop/systemd1", "org.freedesktop.systemd1.Manager")
SETTLE_SECONDS = 2.0
CALL_TIMEOUT_MS = 15000
MAX_TRIES = 5
ROUND_SECONDS = 25
PASS_SECONDS = 5.0
FDS_PER_CALL = 16
SAMPLE_SECONDS = 2.0
NEVER_MOVED = ("konsole",)
WINDOWS = ("/usr/bin/konsole",)
CLIENT = "client"
CLIENT_WORDS = ("attach", "agents")
CLIENT_FLAGS = ("--bg", "--background")
NOT_A_SESSION_FLAGS = ("--version", "-v", "-V", "--help", "-h")
WORKER_RUNTIMES = ("bun", "bun.exe", "node")
WORKER_SCRIPT, WORKER_FOLDER, WORKER_PLUGINS = "worker-service.cjs", "claude-mem", "plugins"


def his_home() -> str:
    try:
        home = pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_dir
    except KeyError:
        return ""
    return os.path.normpath(home) if os.path.isabs(home) else ""


HOME = his_home()
CLAUDE_VERSIONS = os.path.join(HOME, ".local", "share", "claude", "versions") if HOME else ""



class Config:
    def __init__(self, proc: str = "/proc", uid: int = 0, cgroup: str = "/sys/fs/cgroup", record: str = ""):
        self.proc, self.uid, self.cgroup, self.record = proc, uid, cgroup, record
        self.user_prefix = f"/user.slice/user-{uid}.slice/user@{uid}.service/"
        self.lane = self.user_prefix + SLICE

    @classmethod
    def from_env(cls) -> "Config":
        env = os.environ
        return cls(proc=env.get("CLAUDE_HUB_AGENTS_LANE_PROC") or "/proc",
                   uid=int(env.get("CLAUDE_HUB_AGENTS_LANE_UID") or os.getuid()),
                   cgroup=env.get("CLAUDE_HUB_AGENTS_LANE_CGROUP") or "/sys/fs/cgroup",
                   record=env.get("CLAUDE_HUB_AGENTS_LANE_RECORD") or "")

    def in_lane(self, cgroup: str) -> bool:
        return cgroup == self.lane or cgroup.startswith(self.lane + "/")

    def relative(self, cgroup: str) -> str:
        return cgroup[len(self.user_prefix):] if cgroup.startswith(self.user_prefix) else cgroup

    def cgroup_dir(self, *parts: str) -> str:
        return os.path.join(self.cgroup, "user.slice", f"user-{self.uid}.slice",
                            f"user@{self.uid}.service", *parts)

    def path(self, pid: int, name: str) -> str:
        return os.path.join(self.proc, str(pid), name)


class Proc:
    __slots__ = ("pid", "ppid", "comm", "state", "cgroup", "argv", "exe", "start")

    def __init__(self, pid: int, ppid: int, comm: str, state: str, cgroup: str, argv: list[str],
                 exe: str = "", start: int = 0):
        self.pid, self.ppid, self.comm, self.state, self.cgroup, self.argv = pid, ppid, comm, state, cgroup, argv
        self.exe = exe
        self.start = start


def read_text(path: str) -> str:
    with open(path, "rb") as f:
        return f.read().decode("utf-8", "replace")


def read_cgroup(path: str) -> str | None:
    try:
        text = read_text(path)
    except OSError:
        return None
    for line in text.split("\n"):
        if line.startswith("0::"):
            cgroup = line[3:]
            return cgroup[:-len(" (deleted)")] if cgroup.endswith(" (deleted)") else cgroup
    return None


def parse_stat(text: str) -> tuple[str, str, int, int]:
    close = text.rfind(")")
    fields = text[close + 2:].split()
    return text[text.find("(") + 1:close], fields[0], int(fields[1]), int(fields[19])


def read_exe(path: str) -> str:
    try:
        exe = os.readlink(path)
    except OSError:
        return ""
    return exe[:-len(" (deleted)")] if exe.endswith(" (deleted)") else exe


def read_argv(path: str) -> list[str]:
    with open(path, "rb") as f:
        raw = f.read()
    argv = [a.decode("utf-8", "replace") for a in raw.split(b"\0")]
    if argv and argv[-1] == "":
        argv.pop()
    return argv


def scan(cfg: Config) -> dict[int, Proc]:
    procs: dict[int, Proc] = {}
    try:
        names = os.listdir(cfg.proc)
    except OSError:
        return procs
    for name in names:
        if not name.isdigit():
            continue
        pid = int(name)
        cgroup = read_cgroup(cfg.path(pid, "cgroup"))
        if cgroup is None or not cgroup.startswith(cfg.user_prefix):
            continue
        try:
            comm, state, ppid, start = parse_stat(read_text(cfg.path(pid, "stat")))
            argv = read_argv(cfg.path(pid, "cmdline"))
        except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
            continue
        procs[pid] = Proc(pid, ppid, comm, state, cgroup, argv, read_exe(cfg.path(pid, "exe")), start)
    return procs


def owned(cfg: Config, pid: int) -> bool:
    try:
        for line in read_text(cfg.path(pid, "status")).split("\n"):
            if line.startswith("Uid:"):
                return int(line.split()[1]) == cfg.uid
    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
        return os.path.isdir(os.path.join(cfg.proc, str(pid)))
    return True


def same_process(cfg: Config, pid: int, start: int) -> bool:
    try:
        _, state, _, now = parse_stat(read_text(cfg.path(pid, "stat")))
    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
        return False
    return now == start and state not in ("Z", "X")


def now_in(cfg: Config, proc: Proc) -> str | None:
    cgroup = read_cgroup(cfg.path(proc.pid, "cgroup"))
    if cgroup is None:
        return None
    try:
        if read_argv(cfg.path(proc.pid, "cmdline")) != proc.argv or read_exe(cfg.path(proc.pid, "exe")) != proc.exe:
            return None
        comm, state, _, start = parse_stat(read_text(cfg.path(proc.pid, "stat")))
    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
        return None
    return cgroup if start == proc.start and state not in ("Z", "X") and comm == proc.comm else None


def as_scanned(cfg: Config, proc: Proc) -> bool:
    return now_in(cfg, proc) == proc.cgroup



def looks_like_subcommand(word: str) -> bool:
    return word[:1].islower() and word.isascii() and all(c.islower() or c.isdigit() or c == "-" for c in word)


def runs_as_claude(exe: str, argv: list[str]) -> bool:
    if not argv:
        return False
    name = os.path.basename(argv[0].split(" ")[0])
    return name == "claude" or (name != "" and name == os.path.basename(exe))


def is_claude(exe: str, argv: list[str]) -> bool:
    return (bool(exe) and bool(CLAUDE_VERSIONS) and os.path.dirname(exe) == CLAUDE_VERSIONS
            and os.path.basename(exe) != "" and runs_as_claude(exe, argv))


def looks_like_claude(exe: str, argv: list[str]) -> bool:
    if not exe or not runs_as_claude(exe, argv) or is_claude(exe, argv):
        return False
    folder = os.path.dirname(exe)
    return (os.path.basename(exe) == "claude"
            or (os.path.basename(folder) == "versions" and os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(folder)) == "claude"))


def is_worker(exe: str, argv: list[str]) -> bool:
    if os.path.basename(exe) not in WORKER_RUNTIMES or len(argv) < 2 or not HOME:
        return False
    script, home = argv[1], HOME if HOME.endswith("/") else HOME + "/"
    if os.path.basename(script) != WORKER_SCRIPT or os.path.normpath(script) != script or not script.startswith(home):
        return False
    folders = script[len(home):].split("/")[:-1]
    return WORKER_PLUGINS in folders and WORKER_FOLDER in folders[folders.index(WORKER_PLUGINS) + 1:]


def classify(exe: str, argv: list[str]) -> str | None:
    if is_worker(exe, argv):
        return "claude-mem worker"
    if not is_claude(exe, argv):
        return None
    head = argv[0].split(" ")
    rest = head[1:] + argv[1:]
    for word in rest:
        if word == "--":
            break
        if word in CLIENT_WORDS:
            return CLIENT
    if not rest:
        return "claude session"
    first = rest[0]
    if first == "daemon":
        following = rest[1] if len(rest) > 1 else ""
        return "claude daemon" if following in ("", "run") or following.startswith("-") else None
    helper = first.lstrip("-")
    if helper.startswith("bg-") and helper[3:].replace("-", "").isalpha():
        return "claude " + helper
    if looks_like_subcommand(first):
        return None
    if any(a in CLIENT_FLAGS or a in NOT_A_SESSION_FLAGS for a in rest):
        return None
    return "claude session"



class Tree:
    def __init__(self, root: Proc, kind: str, members: list[Proc], origin: str, stray: bool = False, part: int = 0):
        self.root, self.kind = root.pid, kind
        self.root_scanned = root
        self.members = members
        self.origin = origin
        self.stray = stray
        self.part = part

    @property
    def pids(self) -> list[int]:
        return [member.pid for member in self.members]


def children_of(procs: dict[int, Proc]) -> dict[int, list[int]]:
    kids: dict[int, list[int]] = {}
    for pid in sorted(procs):
        kids.setdefault(procs[pid].ppid, []).append(pid)
    return kids


def kinds_of(procs: dict[int, Proc]) -> dict[int, str]:
    kinds = {}
    for pid, proc in procs.items():
        kind = classify(proc.exe, proc.argv)
        if kind:
            kinds[pid] = kind
    return kinds


def staying(procs: dict[int, Proc], kinds: dict[int, str]) -> set[int]:
    return {pid for pid, proc in procs.items()
            if proc.comm in NEVER_MOVED or proc.exe in WINDOWS or kinds.get(pid) == CLIENT}


def subtree(root: int, procs: dict[int, Proc], kids: dict[int, list[int]], stays: set[int]) -> list[int]:
    out, seen = [root], {root}
    i = 0
    while i < len(out):
        for child in kids.get(out[i], ()):
            if child not in seen and child not in stays:
                seen.add(child)
                out.append(child)
        i += 1
    return out


def owning_unit(cfg: Config, cgroup: str) -> str:
    if not cgroup.startswith(cfg.user_prefix):
        return ""
    for part in cgroup[len(cfg.user_prefix):].split("/"):
        if part.endswith((".scope", ".service")):
            return part
    return ""


def movable(cfg: Config, proc: Proc) -> bool:
    return (proc.state not in ("Z", "X") and not cfg.in_lane(proc.cgroup)
            and owning_unit(cfg, proc.cgroup).endswith(".scope") and owned(cfg, proc.pid))


def launched_pid(unit: str) -> int:
    if not (unit.startswith("run-p") and unit.endswith(".scope")):
        return 0
    pid, _, rest = unit[len("run-p"):-len(".scope")].partition("-i")
    return int(pid) if pid.isascii() and pid.isdigit() and rest.isascii() and rest.isdigit() else 0


def window_units(cfg: Config, procs: dict[int, Proc]) -> set[str]:
    windows = {pid: proc for pid, proc in procs.items() if proc.exe in WINDOWS and proc.state not in ("Z", "X")}
    units = set()
    for pid, proc in windows.items():
        unit = owning_unit(cfg, proc.cgroup)
        if unit.endswith(f"-{pid}.scope"):
            units.add(unit)
    oldest: dict[str, int] = {}
    for proc in procs.values():
        unit = owning_unit(cfg, proc.cgroup)
        if launched_pid(unit) in windows:
            oldest[unit] = min(oldest.get(unit, proc.start), proc.start)
    for unit, start in oldest.items():
        if start >= windows[launched_pid(unit)].start:
            units.add(unit)
    return units


def placed(cfg: Config, proc: Proc, units: set[str]) -> bool:
    return owning_unit(cfg, proc.cgroup) not in units


def has_ancestor_in(pid: int, procs: dict[int, Proc], among, stays: set[int]) -> bool:
    seen = {pid}
    parent = procs[pid].ppid
    while parent in procs and parent not in seen:
        if parent in stays:
            return False
        if parent in among:
            return True
        seen.add(parent)
        parent = procs[parent].ppid
    return False


class Plan:

    def __init__(self):
        self.trees: list[Tree] = []
        self.left: list[tuple[int, str, str]] = []
        self.placed: list[tuple[int, str]] = []
        self.placed_trees = 0
        self.lookalikes = 0

    def left_units(self) -> list[str]:
        return sorted({unit for _, _, unit in self.left})

    def placed_units(self) -> list[str]:
        return sorted({unit for _, unit in self.placed})


def plan(cfg: Config, procs: dict[int, Proc]) -> Plan:
    kids = children_of(procs)
    kinds = kinds_of(procs)
    stays = staying(procs, kinds)
    units = window_units(cfg, procs)
    roots = {pid: kind for pid, kind in kinds.items() if kind != CLIENT and pid not in stays}
    ours = {pid for pid in roots if cfg.in_lane(procs[pid].cgroup)
            or (movable(cfg, procs[pid]) and owning_unit(cfg, procs[pid].cgroup) in units)}
    result = Plan()
    result.lookalikes = sum(1 for proc in procs.values() if looks_like_claude(proc.exe, proc.argv))
    placed_at: dict[int, str] = {}

    def count(m: int) -> None:
        placed_at[m] = owning_unit(cfg, procs[m].cgroup) or cfg.relative(procs[m].cgroup)

    for pid in sorted(roots):
        proc = procs[pid]
        if pid in ours:
            if has_ancestor_in(pid, procs, ours, stays):
                continue
            below = []
            for m in subtree(pid, procs, kids, stays)[1:]:
                member = procs[m]
                if member.state in ("Z", "X") or cfg.in_lane(member.cgroup):
                    continue
                if placed(cfg, member, units):
                    if owned(cfg, m):
                        count(m)
                elif movable(cfg, member):
                    below.append(m)
            if not cfg.in_lane(proc.cgroup):
                members, origin, stray = [pid] + below, proc.cgroup, False
            elif below:
                members, origin, stray = below, procs[below[0]].cgroup, True
            else:
                continue
            result.trees.append(Tree(proc, roots[pid], [procs[m] for m in members], cfg.relative(origin), stray))
        elif proc.state in ("Z", "X") or not owned(cfg, pid):
            continue
        elif movable(cfg, proc):
            if has_ancestor_in(pid, procs, ours, stays):
                continue
            for m in subtree(pid, procs, kids, stays | ours):
                member = procs[m]
                if member.state not in ("Z", "X") and not cfg.in_lane(member.cgroup) and owned(cfg, m):
                    count(m)
        elif not has_ancestor_in(pid, procs, roots, stays):
            result.left.append((pid, roots[pid], owning_unit(cfg, proc.cgroup) or cfg.relative(proc.cgroup)))
    result.placed = sorted(placed_at.items())
    tops = {pid for pid in placed_at if pid in roots}
    result.placed_trees = sum(1 for pid in tops if not has_ancestor_in(pid, procs, tops, stays))
    return result



class MoveError(Exception):
    pass


class PidGone(MoveError):
    ...


class NoBus(Exception):
    pass


def gone_in(message: str) -> bool:
    return "UnixProcessIdUnknown" in message or "No such process" in message or "ESRCH" in message


def fits(pins: list) -> None:
    if len(pins) > FDS_PER_CALL:
        raise MoveError(f"{len(pins)} processes in one call: a message on his session bus carries {FDS_PER_CALL}")


class BusMover:

    def __init__(self, cfg: Config, address: str):
        import gi
        gi.require_version("Gio", "2.0")
        from gi.repository import Gio, GLib
        self.cfg, self.Gio, self.GLib = cfg, Gio, GLib
        flags = Gio.DBusConnectionFlags.AUTHENTICATION_CLIENT | Gio.DBusConnectionFlags.MESSAGE_BUS_CONNECTION
        self.bus = Gio.DBusConnection.new_for_address_sync(address, flags, None, None)
        self.bus.set_exit_on_close(False)
        if not self.bus.get_capabilities() & Gio.DBusCapabilityFlags.UNIX_FD_PASSING:
            raise RuntimeError("this bus connection cannot pass file descriptors")

    def pin(self, pid: int) -> int:
        return os.pidfd_open(pid)

    def unpin(self, fd: int) -> None:
        os.close(fd)

    def start_scope(self, unit: str, pins: list[tuple[int, int, int]], description: str) -> list[int]:
        fits(pins)
        V = self.GLib.Variant
        name, path, interface = SYSTEMD
        try:
            fds = self.Gio.UnixFDList.new()
            places = [fds.append(fd) for _, _, fd in pins]
            props = [("Description", V("s", description)), ("Slice", V("s", SLICE)),
                     ("CollectMode", V("s", "inactive-or-failed")),
                     ("OOMPolicy", V("s", "continue")),
                     ("PIDFDs", V("ah", places))]
            self.bus.call_with_unix_fd_list_sync(
                name, path, interface, "StartTransientUnit", V("(ssa(sv)a(sa(sv)))", (unit, "fail", props, [])),
                self.GLib.VariantType("(o)"), self.Gio.DBusCallFlags.NONE, CALL_TIMEOUT_MS, fds, None)
        except self.GLib.Error as err:
            text = str(err.message)
            raise (PidGone if gone_in(text) else MoveError)((text.splitlines() or ["StartTransientUnit"])[0])
        return self.settle(unit, pins)

    def settle(self, unit: str, pins: list[tuple[int, int, int]]) -> list[int]:
        asked = f"{self.cfg.lane}/{unit}"
        end = time.monotonic() + SETTLE_SECONDS
        while True:
            landed, waiting = [], []
            for pid, start, _ in pins:
                cgroup = read_cgroup(self.cfg.path(pid, "cgroup"))
                if cgroup is None or not same_process(self.cfg, pid, start):
                    continue
                if cgroup == asked:
                    landed.append(pid)
                elif not self.cfg.in_lane(cgroup):
                    waiting.append((pid, cgroup))
            if not waiting:
                return landed
            if time.monotonic() >= end:
                if landed:
                    return landed
                pid, cgroup = waiting[0]
                raise MoveError(f"{unit} was queued but process {pid} is still in {self.cfg.relative(cgroup)}")
            time.sleep(0.02)


class RecordingMover:

    def __init__(self, cfg: Config):
        self.cfg = cfg

    def there(self, pid: int) -> bool:
        return os.path.isdir(os.path.join(self.cfg.proc, str(pid)))

    def pin(self, pid: int) -> int:
        if not self.there(pid):
            raise ProcessLookupError(f"no process {pid} in the fake /proc")
        return -1

    def unpin(self, fd: int) -> None:
        pass

    def start_scope(self, unit: str, pins: list[tuple[int, int, int]], description: str) -> list[int]:
        import json
        fits(pins)
        pids = [pid for pid, _, _ in pins]
        gone = [pid for pid in pids if not self.there(pid)]
        with open(self.cfg.record, "a") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps({"call": "StartTransientUnit", "unit": unit, "slice": SLICE, "pids": pids,
                                "starts": [start for _, start, _ in pins], "description": description,
                                "gone": gone}) + "\n")
        if gone:
            raise PidGone("Failed to set unit properties: No such process")
        for pid in pids:
            try:
                with open(self.cfg.path(pid, "cgroup"), "w") as f:
                    f.write(f"0::{self.cfg.lane}/{unit}\n")
            except OSError:
                pass
        return pids


def bus_address(cfg: Config) -> str:
    address = os.environ.get("DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS", "")
    if address:
        return address
    socket_path = os.path.join(os.environ.get("XDG_RUNTIME_DIR") or f"/run/user/{cfg.uid}", "bus")
    return f"unix:path={socket_path}" if os.path.exists(socket_path) else ""


def make_mover(cfg: Config):
    if cfg.record:
        return RecordingMover(cfg)
    if cfg.proc != "/proc":
        raise NoBus("a fake /proc (CLAUDE_HUB_AGENTS_LANE_PROC) is only for the recording mover")
    address = bus_address(cfg)
    if not address:
        raise NoBus("no user bus socket")
    try:
        return BusMover(cfg, address)
    except Exception as err:
        raise NoBus((str(err).splitlines() or [type(err).__name__])[0])



class Outcome:
    def __init__(self, tree: Tree, unit: str):
        self.tree, self.unit = tree, unit
        self.moved: list[int] = []
        self.error = ""


class OutOfTime(Exception):
    ...


class Deadline:

    def __init__(self, clock, seconds: float = ROUND_SECONDS):
        self.clock = clock
        self.ends = clock() + seconds
        self.left = 0

    def check(self) -> None:
        if self.clock() >= self.ends:
            raise OutOfTime()


def pieces(tree: Tree) -> list[Tree]:
    members = tree.members
    cut = [Tree(tree.root_scanned, tree.kind, members[i:i + FDS_PER_CALL], tree.origin, tree.stray, i // FDS_PER_CALL)
           for i in range(0, len(members), FDS_PER_CALL)] or [tree]
    return cut if tree.stray else cut[1:] + cut[:1]


def release(mover, pins: list[tuple[int, int, int]]) -> None:
    for _, _, fd in pins:
        try:
            mover.unpin(fd)
        except OSError:
            pass


def hold(cfg: Config, mover, members: list[Proc], root: Proc) -> list[tuple[int, int, int]] | None:
    try:
        root_hold = mover.pin(root.pid)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return None
    except OSError as err:
        raise MoveError(f"could not take a hold on process {root.pid}: {err.strerror or err}")
    root_pin = (root.pid, root.start, root_hold)
    pins: list[tuple[int, int, int]] = []
    for member in members:
        if member.pid == root.pid:
            continue
        try:
            fd = mover.pin(member.pid)
        except ProcessLookupError:
            continue
        except OSError as err:
            release(mover, pins + [root_pin])
            raise MoveError(f"could not take a hold on process {member.pid}: {err.strerror or err}")
        if as_scanned(cfg, member):
            pins.append((member.pid, member.start, fd))
        else:
            release(mover, [(member.pid, member.start, fd)])
    where = now_in(cfg, root)
    if where is None or not (where == root.cgroup or cfg.in_lane(where)):
        release(mover, pins + [root_pin])
        return None
    if where == root.cgroup and any(member.pid == root.pid for member in members):
        pins.insert(0, root_pin)
    else:
        release(mover, [root_pin])
    return pins


def start_tree(cfg: Config, mover, unit: str, tree: Tree, deadline: Deadline | None = None) -> list[int] | None:
    about = "more of " if tree.part else "strays of " if tree.stray else ""
    description = f"Agent work: {about}{tree.kind} {tree.root} (claude-agents-lane)"
    members = list(tree.members)
    for _ in range(MAX_TRIES):
        if deadline is not None:
            deadline.check()
        pins = hold(cfg, mover, members, tree.root_scanned)
        if pins is None:
            return None
        if not pins:
            return []
        try:
            if deadline is not None:
                deadline.check()
            return mover.start_scope(unit, pins, description)
        except PidGone as err:
            lost = str(err)
        finally:
            release(mover, pins)
        held = {pid for pid, _, _ in pins}
        asked = [member for member in members if member.pid in held]
        members = [member for member in asked if same_process(cfg, member.pid, member.start)]
        if members == asked:
            raise MoveError(f"the manager lost a process ({lost}) while all {len(asked)} it was asked for are still here")
    return None


def adopt_trees(cfg: Config, trees: list[Tree], mover, deadline: Deadline | None = None) -> list[Outcome]:
    outcomes = []
    for n, tree in enumerate(trees):
        for piece in pieces(tree):
            outcome = Outcome(piece, f"agent-{piece.root}-{os.urandom(4).hex()}.scope")
            moved: list[int] | None = []
            try:
                moved = start_tree(cfg, mover, outcome.unit, piece, deadline)
            except OutOfTime:
                deadline.left = len(trees) - n
                return outcomes
            except MoveError as err:
                outcome.error = str(err)
            outcome.moved = moved or []
            outcomes.append(outcome)
            if outcome.error or moved is None:
                break
    return outcomes



OOM_CLAUDE = 400
OOM_OTHER = 600
RLIMITS = {"core": ("Max core file size", "RLIMIT_CORE"), "rtprio": ("Max realtime priority", "RLIMIT_RTPRIO")}


class NoHardener(Exception):
    pass


def limit_word(word: str) -> int:
    return resource.RLIM_INFINITY if word == "unlimited" else int(word)


def parse_limits(text: str) -> dict[str, tuple[int, int]]:
    got: dict[str, tuple[int, int]] = {}
    for line in text.split("\n"):
        for key, (label, _) in RLIMITS.items():
            if line.startswith(label + " "):
                words = line[len(label):].split()
                if len(words) < 2:
                    raise ValueError(f"the {label} line has no soft and hard limit")
                got[key] = (limit_word(words[0]), limit_word(words[1]))
    missing = [label for key, (label, _) in RLIMITS.items() if key not in got]
    if missing:
        raise ValueError(f"no {', '.join(missing)} line in the limits file")
    return got


def wanted(tier: int, adj: int, limits: dict[str, tuple[int, int]]) -> dict:
    todo: dict = {}
    if adj < tier:
        todo["oom_score_adj"] = tier
    for key in RLIMITS:
        soft, hard = limits[key]
        if soft != 0:
            todo[key] = (0, hard)
    return todo


def tier_of(proc: Proc) -> int | None:
    if not proc.exe or not proc.argv:
        return None
    return OOM_CLAUDE if is_claude(proc.exe, proc.argv) else OOM_OTHER


class ProcHardener:

    def __init__(self, cfg: Config):
        self.cfg = cfg

    def bind(self, pid: int) -> int:
        return os.open(os.path.join(self.cfg.proc, str(pid)), os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_CLOEXEC)

    def unbind(self, fd: int) -> None:
        os.close(fd)

    def read(self, fd: int, name: str) -> str:
        f = os.open(name, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=fd)
        try:
            raw = b""
            while chunk := os.read(f, 65536):
                raw += chunk
        finally:
            os.close(f)
        return raw.decode("utf-8", "replace")

    def write_adj(self, fd: int, value: int) -> None:
        f = os.open("oom_score_adj", os.O_WRONLY | os.O_TRUNC | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=fd)
        try:
            os.write(f, f"{value}\n".encode())
        finally:
            os.close(f)

    def set_limit(self, pid: int, which: str, limit: tuple[int, int]) -> None:
        resource.prlimit(pid, getattr(resource, RLIMITS[which][1]), limit)


def on_the_real_proc(path: str) -> bool:
    try:
        return os.stat(path).st_dev == os.stat("/proc").st_dev
    except OSError:
        return True


FAKE_PROC_MARK = "claude-agents-lane-fake-proc"


class RecordingHardener(ProcHardener):

    def __init__(self, cfg: Config):
        super().__init__(cfg)
        self.bound: dict[int, int] = {}
        self.fake_dev = None
        if not on_the_real_proc(cfg.proc):
            import stat
            try:
                marker = os.stat(os.path.join(cfg.proc, FAKE_PROC_MARK), follow_symlinks=False)
                if stat.S_ISREG(marker.st_mode):
                    self.fake_dev = marker.st_dev
            except OSError:
                pass
        self.fake = self.fake_dev is not None

    def bind(self, pid: int) -> int:
        fd = super().bind(pid)
        self.bound[fd] = pid
        return fd

    def unbind(self, fd: int) -> None:
        self.bound.pop(fd, None)
        super().unbind(fd)

    def note(self, line: dict) -> None:
        import json
        with open(self.cfg.record, "a") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps(line) + "\n")

    def overwrite(self, name: str, text: str, dir_fd: int | None = None) -> None:
        import stat
        if self.fake_dev is None:
            return
        info = os.stat(name, dir_fd=dir_fd, follow_symlinks=False)
        if not stat.S_ISREG(info.st_mode) or info.st_dev != self.fake_dev:
            return
        fd = os.open(name, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC, dir_fd=dir_fd)
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
            held = os.fstat(f.fileno())
            if not stat.S_ISREG(held.st_mode) or held.st_dev != self.fake_dev:
                return
            os.ftruncate(f.fileno(), 0)
            f.write(text)

    def write_adj(self, fd: int, value: int) -> None:
        self.overwrite("oom_score_adj", f"{value}\n", fd)
        self.note({"call": "oom_score_adj", "pid": self.bound[fd], "value": value})

    def set_limit(self, pid: int, which: str, limit: tuple[int, int]) -> None:
        if self.fake:
            self.rewrite_limit(pid, which, limit)
        self.note({"call": "set_limit", "pid": pid, "limit": which, "to": list(limit)})

    def rewrite_limit(self, pid: int, which: str, limit: tuple[int, int]) -> None:
        path = self.cfg.path(pid, "limits")
        label = RLIMITS[which][0]
        lines = read_text(path).split("\n")
        for n, line in enumerate(lines):
            if line.startswith(label + " "):
                units = " ".join(line[len(label):].split()[2:])
                soft, hard = ("unlimited" if number == resource.RLIM_INFINITY else str(number) for number in limit)
                lines[n] = f"{label:<25} {soft:<20} {hard:<20} {units:<10}"
        self.overwrite(path, "\n".join(lines))


def make_hardener(cfg: Config):
    if cfg.proc != "/proc" and on_the_real_proc(cfg.proc):
        raise NoHardener("the real /proc under another name (CLAUDE_HUB_AGENTS_LANE_PROC): only /proc itself is hardened")
    if cfg.record:
        return RecordingHardener(cfg)
    if cfg.proc != "/proc":
        raise NoHardener("a fake /proc (CLAUDE_HUB_AGENTS_LANE_PROC) is only for the recording hardener")
    if os.geteuid() != cfg.uid or os.geteuid() == 0:
        raise NoHardener("only his own user may harden his processes")
    return ProcHardener(cfg)


def under_hold(hardener, fd: int) -> tuple[str, int]:
    _, state, _, start = parse_stat(hardener.read(fd, "stat"))
    return state, start


def still_scanned(cfg: Config, hardener, fd: int, proc: Proc) -> bool:
    state, start = under_hold(hardener, fd)
    if start != proc.start or state in ("Z", "X"):
        return False
    cgroup = now_in(cfg, proc)
    return cgroup is not None and cfg.in_lane(cgroup)


def harden_pid(cfg: Config, proc: Proc, tier: int, hardener, result: dict) -> None:
    try:
        fd = hardener.bind(proc.pid)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        result["failed"] += 1
        return
    done = 0
    try:
        try:
            adj = int(hardener.read(fd, "oom_score_adj"))
            todo = wanted(tier, adj, parse_limits(hardener.read(fd, "limits")))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            result["failed"] += 1
            return
        for what, value in todo.items():
            try:
                if not still_scanned(cfg, hardener, fd, proc):
                    break
                if what == "oom_score_adj":
                    hardener.write_adj(fd, value)
                else:
                    hardener.set_limit(proc.pid, what, value)
            except Exception:
                result["failed"] += 1
                continue
            if what != "oom_score_adj":
                try:
                    hit = under_hold(hardener, fd)[1] == proc.start
                except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
                    hit = False
                if not hit:
                    result["failed"] += 1
                    break
            done += 1
    finally:
        try:
            hardener.unbind(fd)
        except OSError:
            pass
        if done:
            result["hardened"] += 1


def below_a_window(pid: int, procs: dict[int, Proc], kinds: dict[int, str], stays: set[int]) -> bool:
    seen: set[int] = set()
    while pid in procs:
        if pid in seen:
            return True
        seen.add(pid)
        if pid in stays:
            return True
        if pid in kinds:
            return False
        pid = procs[pid].ppid
    return False


def harden_lane(cfg: Config, procs: dict[int, Proc], hardener, budget) -> dict:
    result = {"hardened": 0, "failed": 0, "out_of_time": False}
    kinds = kinds_of(procs)
    stays = staying(procs, kinds)
    for pid in sorted(procs):
        proc = procs[pid]
        if not cfg.in_lane(proc.cgroup) or proc.state in ("Z", "X") or below_a_window(pid, procs, kinds, stays):
            continue
        tier = tier_of(proc)
        if tier is None or not owned(cfg, pid):
            continue
        try:
            budget.check()
        except OutOfTime:
            result["out_of_time"] = True
            break
        harden_pid(cfg, proc, tier, hardener, result)
    return result



def describe(verb: str, tree: Tree, size: int, destination: str) -> str:
    if tree.part:
        what = f"{size} more process(es) of {tree.kind} {tree.root}"
    elif tree.stray:
        what = f"{size} stray process(es) of {tree.kind} {tree.root}"
    else:
        what = f"{tree.kind} {tree.root} (+{max(size - 1, 0)})"
    return f"{verb} {what} from {tree.origin} -> {destination}"


def cmd_adopt(cfg: Config, flags: set[str], mover=None, clock=None) -> int:
    deadline = Deadline(clock or time.monotonic)
    dry_run, as_json = "--dry-run" in flags, "--json" in flags
    procs = scan(cfg)
    planned = plan(cfg, procs)
    trees, left = planned.trees, planned.left_units()
    report: dict = {"dry_run": dry_run, "adopted": [], "errors": [],
                    "left": {"trees": len(planned.left), "units": left}, "lookalikes": planned.lookalikes,
                    "placed": len(planned.placed), "placed_trees": planned.placed_trees}

    def finish(code: int) -> int:
        if as_json:
            import json
            print(json.dumps(report))
        return code

    if dry_run:
        for tree in (piece for whole in trees for piece in pieces(whole)):
            to = f"{SLICE}/agent-{tree.root}-*.scope"
            report["adopted"].append({"kind": tree.kind, "pid": tree.root, "processes": len(tree.members),
                                      "stray": tree.stray, "part": tree.part, "from": tree.origin, "to": to})
            if not as_json:
                print(describe("would adopt", tree, len(tree.members), to), flush=True)
        if planned.left and not as_json:
            print(f"would leave {len(planned.left)} tree(s) where they are, in units that are not scopes: "
                  f"{', '.join(left)}", flush=True)
        if planned.placed and not as_json:
            among = f", {planned.placed_trees} whole agent tree(s) among them" if planned.placed_trees else ""
            print(f"would leave {len(planned.placed)} process(es) in {len(planned.placed_units())} unit(s) where "
                  f"somebody put them{among}", flush=True)
        return finish(0)
    seconds = min(PASS_SECONDS, deadline.ends - deadline.clock())
    if seconds > 0:
        try:
            harden_lane(cfg, procs, make_hardener(cfg), Deadline(deadline.clock, seconds))
        except Exception:
            pass
    if not trees:
        return finish(0)
    if mover is None:
        try:
            mover = make_mover(cfg)
        except NoBus as err:
            note = f"claude-agents-lane: no session bus ({err}); {len(trees)} tree(s) not moved"
            report["errors"].append(note)
            print(note, file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
            return finish(0)
    failed = False
    for outcome in adopt_trees(cfg, trees, mover, deadline):
        tree = outcome.tree
        if outcome.error:
            failed = True
            note = f"claude-agents-lane: could not adopt {tree.kind} {tree.root}: {outcome.error}"
            report["errors"].append(note)
            print(note, file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        if not outcome.moved:
            continue
        to = f"{SLICE}/{outcome.unit}"
        report["adopted"].append({"kind": tree.kind, "pid": tree.root, "processes": len(outcome.moved),
                                  "stray": tree.stray, "part": tree.part, "from": tree.origin, "to": to,
                                  "unit": outcome.unit})
        if not as_json:
            print(describe("adopted", tree, len(outcome.moved), to), flush=True)
    if deadline.left:
        failed = True
        note = (f"claude-agents-lane: the round's {ROUND_SECONDS} s ran out; {deadline.left} tree(s) not reached "
                "or not finished, left for the next round")
        report["errors"].append(note)
        print(note, file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
    return finish(1 if failed else 0)


def read_number(path: str) -> int | None:
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            return int(f.read().split()[0])
    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
        return None


def usage_usec(directory: str) -> int | None:
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(directory, "cpu.stat")) as f:
            for line in f.read().splitlines():
                if line.startswith("usage_usec"):
                    return int(line.split()[1])
    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
        pass
    return None


def agents_inside(cfg: Config, procs: dict[int, Proc]) -> int:
    kids = children_of(procs)
    kinds = kinds_of(procs)
    stays = staying(procs, kinds)
    members: set[int] = set()
    for pid, kind in kinds.items():
        if kind != CLIENT and pid not in stays:
            members.update(subtree(pid, procs, kids, stays))
    return sum(1 for m in members if procs[m].state not in ("Z", "X") and cfg.in_lane(procs[m].cgroup))


def lane_status(cfg: Config, sleep=time.sleep) -> dict:
    procs = scan(cfg)
    planned = plan(cfg, procs)
    lane_dir = cfg.cgroup_dir(SLICE)
    status: dict = {"lane": SLICE, "exists": os.path.isdir(lane_dir),
                    "weight": read_number(os.path.join(lane_dir, "cpu.weight")),
                    "inside": agents_inside(cfg, procs), "outside": sum(len(tree.members) for tree in planned.trees),
                    "outside_trees": len(planned.trees),
                    "left_trees": len(planned.left), "left_units": planned.left_units(),
                    "placed": len(planned.placed), "placed_units": len(planned.placed_units()),
                    "placed_trees": planned.placed_trees, "lookalikes": planned.lookalikes,
                    "siblings": {}, "cpu_share": None, "lane_cores": None, "user_cores": None,
                    "sample_seconds": SAMPLE_SECONDS}
    for name in ("app.slice", "session.slice", "background.slice"):
        weight = read_number(cfg.cgroup_dir(name, "cpu.weight"))
        if weight is not None:
            status["siblings"][name] = weight
    if not status["exists"]:
        return status
    user_dir = cfg.cgroup_dir()
    before = (usage_usec(lane_dir), usage_usec(user_dir))
    started = time.monotonic()
    sleep(SAMPLE_SECONDS)
    elapsed = max(time.monotonic() - started, 1e-6)
    after = (usage_usec(lane_dir), usage_usec(user_dir))
    if None not in before + after:
        lane_used, user_used = after[0] - before[0], after[1] - before[1]
        status["lane_cores"] = round(lane_used / 1e6 / elapsed, 2)
        status["user_cores"] = round(user_used / 1e6 / elapsed, 2)
        status["cpu_share"] = round(lane_used / user_used, 4) if user_used > 0 else 0.0
    return status


def cmd_status(cfg: Config, flags: set[str], sleep=time.sleep) -> int:
    s = lane_status(cfg, sleep)
    if "--json" in flags:
        import json
        print(json.dumps(s))
        return 0
    siblings = ", ".join(f"{name} {weight}" for name, weight in s["siblings"].items())
    if not s["exists"]:
        weight = f"not created yet (nothing has been moved into {SLICE})"
    elif s["weight"] == WANTED_WEIGHT:
        weight = f"{s['weight']}" + (f"  (beside {siblings})" if siblings else "")
    else:
        weight = (f"{s['weight']}, not the {WANTED_WEIGHT} it should be: link agents.slice into "
                  f"~/.config/systemd/user and run systemctl --user daemon-reload")
    print(f"{SLICE} cpu.weight   {weight}")
    outside = f"{s['outside']} outside it"
    if s["outside"]:
        outside += f" in {s['outside_trees']} tree(s); claude-agents-lane adopt moves them"
    print(f"agent processes      {s['inside']} inside the lane, {outside}")
    if s["left_trees"]:
        print(f"left where they are  {s['left_trees']} tree(s) in units that are not scopes: "
              f"{', '.join(s['left_units'])}")
    if s["placed"]:
        among = f", {s['placed_trees']} whole agent tree(s) among them" if s["placed_trees"] else ""
        print(f"placed elsewhere     {s['placed']} process(es) in {s['placed_units']} unit(s), left where somebody "
              f"put them{among}")
    if s["lookalikes"]:
        print(f"look-alikes          {s['lookalikes']} process(es) that look like Claude but are not in his install "
              "folder: never moved")
    if s["cpu_share"] is None:
        print("lane share of CPU    n/a (no lane to sample)")
    else:
        print(f"lane share of CPU    {s['cpu_share'] * 100:.1f}% of his user CPU over {s['sample_seconds']:.0f} s "
              f"({s['lane_cores']} of {s['user_cores']} cores busy)")
    return 0


COMMANDS = {"adopt": {"--dry-run", "--json"}, "status": {"--json"}}


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None, *, mover=None, sleep=time.sleep, clock=None) -> int:
    argv = sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else list(argv)
    if argv[:1] in (["-h"], ["--help"], ["help"]):
        print(__doc__.strip())
        return 0
    if not argv or argv[0] not in COMMANDS or not set(argv[1:]) <= COMMANDS[argv[0]]:
        print(__doc__.strip(), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    cfg, flags = Config.from_env(), set(argv[1:])
    if argv[0] == "adopt":
        return cmd_adopt(cfg, flags, mover, clock)
    return cmd_status(cfg, flags, sleep)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        sys.exit(main())
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        sys.exit(130)
